# __PROJECT_NAME__ docs

__ONE_LINER__

This is the knowledge base agents and humans read **before implementing**, so new
work follows the existing architecture, constraints, and decisions. Read
selectively: open what the task needs, not everything.

Work is delivered per version with the Agentic SDD process
(`/engineer:requirement` → `plan` → `architect` → `build` → `release`); see
`04-conventions/git-workflow.md` and `/engineer:guide`.

## Reading order

1. `00-context/` — what the product is and the shared vocabulary.
2. `02-constraints/invariants.md` — the rules you must never break. Always check.
3. `03-decisions/` — decisions already made and why. Find the ones tagged for
   your area before proposing anything.
4. The architecture + conventions files relevant to your task (map below).

## When to read what

| If your task touches…            | Read…                                                        |
|----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| Anything, always                 | `02-constraints/invariants.md`                               |
| Overall structure / a new module | `01-architecture/overview.md`, then the relevant `components/`|
| Data, schema, migrations         | `01-architecture/data-model.md`                              |
| An external API or endpoint      | `04-conventions/api-design.md`                               |
| Adding/updating a dependency     | `02-constraints/dependencies.md`                             |
| Performance / security / limits  | `02-constraints/non-functional.md`                           |
| Tests                            | `04-conventions/testing.md`                                  |
| Code layout / naming / patterns  | `04-conventions/coding-style.md`                             |
| Branches / commits / PRs         | `04-conventions/git-workflow.md`                             |
| Current behaviour of a feature   | `test-cases/feature-tests/<domain>/` (living spec, Gherkin)  |
| The version you are working on   | `plans/vX.Y.Z.T/` — requirement, plan, architecture          |

## Status markers

- An ADR is binding only when `status: Accepted`. `Proposed` means under
  discussion — do not treat it as a rule yet.
- A feature test describes current behaviour only while `status: active`.
- A version's plan files are binding only for that version; check the
  `status:` in its `requirement.md`.
- `TODO: confirm` marks content that was scaffolded but not yet verified.

## Conventions for these docs

- Markdown + YAML frontmatter + Mermaid only, so everything is greppable.
- Reference things by ID: invariants `INV-00x`, decisions `ADR-000x`,
  requirements `REQ-NN` / goals `G-NN` (per version), feature tests
  `FT-vX.Y.Z.T-NN`.
- Architecture/description docs follow the code. Constraints and ADRs lead the
  code — if code conflicts with them, fix the code or change the decision
  deliberately, don't rewrite the rule to match the code.
